<article class="env-lemma" id="0EE6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EE6">Lemma <span data-tag="0EE6">82.4.5</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EDT" data-tag="0EDT">82.2.1</a> let $X/B$ be good. Let $T \subset |X|$ be a closed subset and $t \in T$. If $\dim _\delta (T) \leq k$ and $\delta (t) = k$, then $t$ is a generic point of an irreducible component of $T$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We know $t$ is contained in an irreducible component $T' \subset T$. Let $t' \in T'$ be the generic point. Then $k \geq \delta (t') \geq \delta (t)$. Since $\delta $ is a dimension function we see that $t = t'$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>